1. Simple Logic

We know the majority element appears more than n/2 times.

Think of the array as a voting/cancellation game:

Pick one number as the candidate.

If we see the same number, it gets +1 vote.
If we see a different number, it gets -1 vote.

When the count becomes 0, choose the next number as the new candidate.
Since the majority element is guaranteed to exist, the final candidate is the answer.


Remember:
Same number      → count + 1
Different number → count - 1
count == 0       → new candidate
